{
  "analysis": "We are in /app with an empty/unknown workspace and no project created yet. We need to create a Python package named mathutils with an add() function, configure pyproject.toml to use the uv_build backend (PEP 732 editable-build mechanism as requested), build with `uv build`, then install in editable mode with `uv pip install --editable .`, and verify that changing the source affects behavior without reinstalling.",
  "plan": "1) Inspect the directory and confirm uv/python availability. 2) Create a minimal package layout: pyproject.toml + mathutils/__init__.py. 3) Configure build-system to use uv_build (requires uv-build, build-backend uv_build). 4) Create a virtual environment and use `uv pip` inside it. 5) Run `uv build` to confirm the backend works. 6) Install editable with `uv pip install --editable .`. 7) Verify import + add(). 8) Modify source and re-run the import in a new Python process to prove editable reflects changes without reinstalling.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 --version\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv --version\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > pyproject.toml <<'EOF'\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"uv-build\"]\nbuild-backend = \"uv_build\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"mathutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Small math utilities\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = {text = \"MIT\"}\nauthors = [{name = \"Example\"}]\n\n[tool.uv]\n# no runtime dependencies\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# mathutils\n\nA tiny example package.\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > mathutils/__init__.py <<'EOF'\n\"\"\"mathutils package.\"\"\"\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Add two numbers together.\"\"\"\n    return a + b\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find . -maxdepth 2 -type f -print\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv venv\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv build\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv pip install --editable .\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils; print('add(1,2)=', mathutils.add(1,2))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils, inspect; import os; print('mathutils file:', os.path.abspath(mathutils.__file__))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "perl -0777 -i -pe 's/return a \\+ b/return a + b + 100/' mathutils/__init__.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils; print('after edit add(1,2)=', mathutils.add(1,2))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": true
}

{
  "analysis": "uv-build is failing because it expects a `src/`-layout package (`src/mathutils/__init__.py`), but the package currently lives at `/app/mathutils/__init__.py`. Also, our import tests succeeded only because Python imported the local `/app/mathutils` package from the current working directory, not from an installed editable wheel. We need to move the package under `src/`, rebuild with `uv build`, then do `uv pip install --editable .`, and verify from a different directory (e.g. /tmp) that imports come from the editable install and reflect source changes without reinstalling.",
  "plan": "1) Remove the top-level `mathutils/` package that is masking the installed import. 2) Create `src/mathutils/__init__.py` with the add() function. 3) Re-run `uv build` to confirm uv_build can build sdist/wheel. 4) Install editable with `uv pip install --editable .` (uninstall first if needed). 5) Verify from `/tmp` that `mathutils.__file__` points into `/app/src/...` (editable). 6) Edit the source under `src/` and re-run the `/tmp` import to confirm the change is reflected without reinstalling.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -rf mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p src/mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > src/mathutils/__init__.py <<'EOF'\n\"\"\"mathutils package.\"\"\"\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Add two numbers together.\"\"\"\n    return a + b\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find . -maxdepth 3 -type f -print\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv build\n",
      "duration": 6.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv pip uninstall -y mathutils || true\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv pip install --editable .\n",
      "duration": 6.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils, os; print('add(1,2)=', mathutils.add(1,2)); print('mathutils file:', os.path.abspath(mathutils.__file__))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "perl -0777 -i -pe 's/return a \\+ b/return a + b + 100/' /app/src/mathutils/__init__.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils; print('after edit add(1,2)=', mathutils.add(1,2))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

